WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:03.650
The demon army will be attacking soon.

00:05.020 --> 00:08.770
Are you telling me a war is about to start?

00:08.770 --> 00:10.050
That's right.

00:10.050 --> 00:15.460
You're going to be on the front lines 
with me, healing the wounded.

00:16.230 --> 00:18.110
We'll be part of the vanguard.

00:18.540 --> 00:21.030
Th-The vanguard? Me?

00:21.300 --> 00:22.850
But what about Tong and the others?

00:22.850 --> 00:25.470
I heard there are other healers, too.

00:25.470 --> 00:28.860
Yeah, there are two more, 
but they have a different role.

00:28.860 --> 00:30.380
The right man for the right job.

00:30.380 --> 00:34.580
B-But I don't think I can do what you do...

00:34.580 --> 00:37.520
Well, we have a little more time.

00:37.520 --> 00:39.910
Steel yourself before it runs out.

00:42.400 --> 00:46.210
<i>Can I really do something like that?</i>

01:01.580 --> 01:06.250
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

02:17.070 --> 02:20.950
#4 Rescue Team Member Usato!

02:22.030 --> 02:25.370
How go the preparations to 
invade the Llinger Kingdom?

02:25.660 --> 02:27.260
Proceeding smoothly.

02:28.040 --> 02:31.770
Our units have finished preparing for battle.

02:32.650 --> 02:35.660
We shall soon begin our advance.

02:36.010 --> 02:39.480
I see. I'll have you lead the troops.

02:39.480 --> 02:43.370
Despite our previous successes, 
they managed to escape our grasp before.

02:43.370 --> 02:46.690
You needn't fight to the death, 
but I do expect your utmost effort.

02:46.690 --> 02:49.430
I will do my best.

02:49.650 --> 02:52.450
You're always so serious, Amila.

02:52.450 --> 02:54.460
No matter. You're dismissed.

02:54.460 --> 02:55.250
Sire.

03:00.910 --> 03:07.790
Oh, my. Was the third army commander
nervous in front of the Demon Lord?

03:07.790 --> 03:12.710
If you have time to mock others, 
then focus on your work, demon doctor.

03:12.710 --> 03:15.030
Stop using that weird nickname!

03:15.030 --> 03:18.060
Call me by my proper name, Hyriluk.

03:19.970 --> 03:23.090
And I'll have you know my work 
is proceeding quite smoothly.

03:23.090 --> 03:26.490
I just completed the newest 
demon-made monster prototype.

03:26.900 --> 03:28.260
Want to come see?

03:30.180 --> 03:31.410
What do you think?

03:31.410 --> 03:34.820
It's highly venomous and has 
a large body with sharp fangs.

03:34.820 --> 03:38.620
I call it Demon-Made Monster 
Prototype 72, Baljinak!

03:39.040 --> 03:42.180
You gave Prototype 71 the same name.

03:42.180 --> 03:46.770
Didn't it go missing when we attacked 
the Llinger Kingdom last time?

03:46.770 --> 03:51.780
It ran away after being wounded 
by an enemy named Siglis.

03:52.190 --> 03:55.930
It's all right! Number 72 is much stronger!

03:55.930 --> 03:57.450
I hope that's true.

03:57.450 --> 04:02.060
There are people more troublesome 
than Siglis in Llinger.

04:03.410 --> 04:08.870
Are you talking about the <i>kidnappers</i>? 
I've heard rumors about them.

04:09.080 --> 04:10.190
That's right.

04:10.190 --> 04:12.910
They stand on the battlefield but don't fight.

04:12.910 --> 04:16.280
They carry the injured away to 
the rear before you realize it.

04:16.540 --> 04:20.000
In other words, they minimize
their own casualties.

04:20.000 --> 04:23.280
And their boss is a healer who runs around

04:23.780 --> 04:27.370
all over the front lines, 
healing people on the spot.

04:27.370 --> 04:31.900
She's a top-notch fighter, too. 
Infuriatingly so.

04:32.470 --> 04:35.300
That woman holds a deep
 grudge against my master.

04:35.920 --> 04:37.600
One day, I swear I'll...

04:38.290 --> 04:39.710
I see.

04:39.710 --> 04:45.060
But you're the commander this time, 
so you can't go into battle yourself.

04:45.060 --> 04:46.630
I know that.

04:46.630 --> 04:48.960
I plan to send that demon...

04:49.590 --> 04:53.300
The immortal mage of darkness, 
the Black Knight.

04:59.750 --> 05:02.220
Beds are the best!

05:02.220 --> 05:05.450
I even missed hearing Tong's snoring.

05:08.790 --> 05:11.050
Hey, you awake?

05:14.690 --> 05:16.070
Time for breakfast.

05:16.070 --> 05:18.790
I brought you a few things
from the cafeteria.

05:18.790 --> 05:21.350
This is probably some kind of fruit.

05:24.470 --> 05:26.240
You make it look so delicious!

05:26.240 --> 05:27.380
I'll have one, too.

05:29.470 --> 05:31.950
Hey, it tastes better than it looks!

05:35.030 --> 05:36.590
You're such a glutton.

05:39.730 --> 05:41.440
You traitor.

05:41.440 --> 05:45.330
I haven't forgotten how you toyed
with my pure, innocent heart.

05:46.660 --> 05:48.150
So cute...

05:48.150 --> 05:49.340
No, no, no!

05:49.340 --> 05:52.290
You won't fool me again,
 no matter how cute you are!

05:58.270 --> 06:01.300
Fine, fine! You can have some, too!

06:05.410 --> 06:08.210
I know. You're cute, too.

06:08.210 --> 06:10.210
Eat up, Blurin.

06:10.210 --> 06:12.220
Blurin?

06:12.950 --> 06:14.220
Oh, Captain Rose.

06:14.220 --> 06:16.390
Is that what you named it?

06:16.620 --> 06:18.050
That's right.

06:18.050 --> 06:21.510
I took the "blu" from blue and "ri" 
from grizzly to make "Blurin."

06:21.510 --> 06:25.820
Pretty good name, if I do say 
so myself. Right, Blurin?

06:27.330 --> 06:32.860
Uh, Mr. Blurin, that's my hand you're 
trying to eat... It kinda hurts...

06:32.860 --> 06:34.030
Well, whatever.

06:34.030 --> 06:37.280
I reported the bear to His Majesty.

06:37.280 --> 06:40.330
We have permission to keep him 
as property of the Rescue Team.

06:40.330 --> 06:42.080
P-Property?

06:42.080 --> 06:43.380
That's how it is.

06:43.380 --> 06:48.670
You can stay, but you have to earn your keep.

06:54.760 --> 06:56.650
What do you want Blurin to do?

06:58.680 --> 06:59.810
Huh?

07:01.340 --> 07:03.380
Why am I carrying him?

07:03.380 --> 07:05.770
I could understand running together, but...

07:05.770 --> 07:08.710
This is simulation training.

07:08.960 --> 07:13.490
Think of that bear as someone
who needs to be rescued.

07:14.020 --> 07:16.350
Someone who needs to be rescued?

07:16.750 --> 07:18.570
In other words, a wounded soldier.

07:18.570 --> 07:20.270
Now hurry up and get running!

07:20.270 --> 07:21.190
Y-Yes, ma'am!

07:21.190 --> 07:22.430
Let's go, Blurin!

07:23.170 --> 07:26.840
This just means I have more weight to carry.

07:27.040 --> 07:30.340
It'll be a breeze if I manage my mana as I run.

07:30.340 --> 07:33.710
Pick up the pace! The wounded 
soldier isn't gonna make it!

07:34.960 --> 07:37.690
<i>I can't help how heavy
the little guy is! Jeez...</i>

07:42.590 --> 07:44.470
What the hell are you guys doing?!

07:45.070 --> 07:47.190
Didn't the boss tell you?

07:47.190 --> 07:50.150
We're simulating the battlefield!

07:50.150 --> 07:51.490
I don't need your help!

07:51.490 --> 07:54.270
The others are waiting to ambush you, too!

07:54.270 --> 07:56.270
Better stay focused!

07:56.270 --> 07:57.400
Damn it!

07:57.410 --> 07:59.330
<b>One Hour Later</b>

07:57.410 --> 07:59.330
<b>One Hour Later</b>

08:06.540 --> 08:08.080
That reeks! What the hell?!

08:08.080 --> 08:10.220
That's my special stink water!

08:10.220 --> 08:12.140
Don't make weird things!

08:12.130 --> 08:14.090
<b>Three Hours Later</b>

08:12.130 --> 08:14.090
<b>Three Hours Later</b>

08:17.510 --> 08:20.430
<b>Four Hours Later</b>

08:17.510 --> 08:20.430
<b>Four Hours Later</b>

08:18.060 --> 08:20.420
<i>Huh? I feel kinda...</i>

08:23.450 --> 08:24.680
You, too?!

08:30.320 --> 08:33.850
<i>That's weird... What's happening?</i>

08:41.420 --> 08:42.850
Thanks.

08:43.820 --> 08:47.010
I thought I'd be able to manage 
for at least half a day...

08:47.010 --> 08:49.840
That's the limit of your 
endurance on the battlefield.

08:49.840 --> 08:50.760
Huh?

08:51.010 --> 08:58.340
Humans feel exhaustion from 
nervousness, fear, and impatience.

08:58.340 --> 09:01.760
That's why you ran out of 
strength faster than normal.

09:01.760 --> 09:03.380
Then what am I supposed to—

09:03.380 --> 09:04.690
Get used to it.

09:04.690 --> 09:08.590
Acquire mental fortitude and decisiveness 
that don't falter in the face of fear.

09:09.990 --> 09:11.760
Thank you very much.

09:11.760 --> 09:14.090
Once your mana has recovered,

09:14.090 --> 09:16.910
spend the afternoon running
around the castle town.

09:16.910 --> 09:19.450
Huh? While carrying Blurin?

09:20.410 --> 09:21.620
Of course.

09:22.200 --> 09:23.790
What?

09:25.710 --> 09:27.570
Hey, look at that.

09:27.570 --> 09:29.260
A blue grizzly?!

09:29.260 --> 09:30.830
Hey! That's bad news!

09:31.180 --> 09:33.160
<i>I figured as much.</i>

09:33.160 --> 09:35.950
<i>Blurin may be docile,
but he's still a monster.</i>

09:35.950 --> 09:38.090
<i>Of course he'd cause a commotion.</i>

09:38.090 --> 09:40.510
Say, now that I took a good look...

09:40.510 --> 09:42.920
Oh, he's one of them.

09:42.920 --> 09:44.800
Man, I got all scared for nothing.

09:44.800 --> 09:45.930
<i>Huh?</i>

09:53.520 --> 09:55.250
What is it, Blurin?

09:57.630 --> 09:59.080
Welcome.

09:59.080 --> 10:01.480
How about some fresh fruit?

10:01.480 --> 10:05.360
I'm sorry. I don't have any money, 
so I can't buy anything.

10:05.360 --> 10:07.510
What are these fruits called?

10:07.510 --> 10:13.080
Oh, these are peffles. 
They're a specialty of this kingdom.

10:14.740 --> 10:17.690
Um, could I ask one more question?

10:19.190 --> 10:22.920
I'm carrying a monster on my back. 
Why is everyone so calm?

10:22.920 --> 10:25.780
That's because you're a 
part of the Rescue Team.

10:25.780 --> 10:28.000
We can tell by your clothes.

10:28.640 --> 10:30.470
Well, that's true...

10:30.470 --> 10:35.410
We see scary-looking men from the Rescue 
Team running around town all the time.

10:35.410 --> 10:38.020
Hardly anything fazes us now.

10:40.130 --> 10:44.410
<i>Yeah, if you can get used to their scary 
faces, what else could scare you?</i>

10:45.740 --> 10:49.720
Thank you very much. 
I'll buy some fruit next time!

10:49.720 --> 10:52.850
Since we've gotten acquainted, 
this one's my treat.

10:52.850 --> 10:54.910
Huh? Are you sure?

10:55.720 --> 10:57.260
Lucky us, Blurin!

10:57.260 --> 11:00.630
Hey, that's bad manners!

11:01.540 --> 11:04.770
Thanks so much. See you next time!

11:06.530 --> 11:09.060
Was that boy from the Rescue Team?

11:09.600 --> 11:13.920
Seems so. Is something the matter, Amako?

11:14.410 --> 11:16.190
No, it's nothing.

11:22.550 --> 11:26.690
Since we're close to the castle grounds, 
we should visit Kazuki and Senpai.

11:27.220 --> 11:28.870
What do you think, Blurin?

11:30.070 --> 11:32.690
Yeah, you're right. Let's do it.

11:36.900 --> 11:40.370
Wait, will I be allowed to 
take Blurin into the castle?

11:37.070 --> 11:39.920
Y-You there! Excuse me...

11:40.370 --> 11:43.760
Since the king lives there, 
maybe they'll say no...

11:40.430 --> 11:43.420
Wait a second! Hey!

11:43.760 --> 11:46.090
Nah, just look at how cute he is.

11:46.090 --> 11:48.350
You there... from the Rescue Team...

11:46.090 --> 11:49.290
Maybe I could pass him off as a big 
stuffed animal. No, maybe not...

11:51.090 --> 11:53.870
Hey, are you all right?

11:57.190 --> 11:58.620
How do you feel?

11:59.070 --> 12:02.250
A lot better. Sorry for the trouble.

12:02.250 --> 12:06.360
Don't mention it. Anyway, 
were you trying to get my attention?

12:06.360 --> 12:09.810
Yes. I wanted to say hello to my new junior.

12:10.210 --> 12:12.790
I don't usually raise my voice like that.

12:12.790 --> 12:14.380
Your junior?

12:14.380 --> 12:17.100
Oh, the captain didn't tell you?

12:17.530 --> 12:19.480
My name's Orga Fleur.

12:19.480 --> 12:24.260
I'm one of the Rescue Team's healers.
 Nice to meet you.

12:22.090 --> 12:26.010
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

12:26.730 --> 12:30.790
Huh... I knew that we had a new member,

12:30.790 --> 12:33.940
but I never would've guessed you 
were summoned with the heroes.

12:34.220 --> 12:36.460
Well, it's true.

12:36.460 --> 12:40.600
Though I've been training so much
every day that I'd nearly forgotten myself.

12:42.380 --> 12:46.750
Usato, it's amazing that you can 
keep up with the captain's training.

12:46.750 --> 12:49.570
It was impossible for me and my sister.

12:49.570 --> 12:51.130
Your sister?

12:51.130 --> 12:53.740
Oh, is she the other healer?

12:54.050 --> 12:57.210
Yeah, she's five years younger than me.

12:57.970 --> 13:01.720
We run a clinic in the city.

13:01.720 --> 13:05.310
We use our healing magic
to heal the citizens.

13:06.100 --> 13:07.210
Oh....

13:07.210 --> 13:10.000
Huh? But you collapsed earlier...

13:11.290 --> 13:15.590
To tell you the truth,
 I'm not very good at healing myself.

13:15.590 --> 13:18.390
I'm much better at healing other people.

13:18.390 --> 13:22.110
I guess there are all kinds of healers, huh?

13:22.110 --> 13:22.860
Yeah.

13:22.860 --> 13:26.380
But we're still a part of the Rescue Team.

13:26.380 --> 13:30.610
We work under the captain and tend 
to the wounded in times of need.

13:31.050 --> 13:32.330
In times of need...

13:32.600 --> 13:37.960
You're going to be on the front lines 
with me, healing the wounded.

13:38.740 --> 13:40.700
We'll be part of the vanguard.

13:42.300 --> 13:46.890
Um, what do you do on the battlefield?

13:48.140 --> 13:53.720
Well, Tong and the others bring 
the injured soldiers to the rear,

13:53.720 --> 13:56.880
where my sister and I heal them.

13:57.150 --> 13:59.350
In other words, we're support members.

13:59.740 --> 14:04.250
Captain Rose actually asked me
 to join her as part of the vanguard.

14:04.250 --> 14:06.160
What? Really?

14:06.160 --> 14:07.200
Yes.

14:07.200 --> 14:10.720
But can I really handle that?

14:13.610 --> 14:17.600
In battle, the knights and heroes
who fight on the front lines

14:17.600 --> 14:19.780
are always in the greatest danger.

14:22.630 --> 14:27.990
When they fall injured and get left behind,
normally all they can do is wait for death.

14:27.990 --> 14:34.800
But if there are healers running around 
on the battlefield, they can be saved.

14:35.390 --> 14:39.230
Of course, it's a dangerous 
and exhausting job...

14:40.080 --> 14:45.680
But the captain wouldn't choose 
someone she didn't completely trust.

14:48.440 --> 14:53.590
Well, I need to get back to the clinic 
or my little sister will scold me.

14:53.590 --> 14:54.850
Oh, sure.

14:54.850 --> 14:56.720
I'll get back to training.

14:57.510 --> 15:00.300
I'm glad we got to talk, Usato.

15:00.690 --> 15:02.740
Before you go, may I ask one thing?

15:02.740 --> 15:04.300
What is it?

15:04.560 --> 15:07.860
Please don't hate Captain Rose too much.

15:07.860 --> 15:10.710
I can't say she's kind by any 
stretch of the imagination...

15:10.970 --> 15:14.070
But, well... She's just clumsy 
with people. That's all.

15:14.070 --> 15:15.050
Don't worry.

15:15.730 --> 15:17.790
I never hated her.

15:17.790 --> 15:20.860
Even if I do have a bone or two to pick.

15:20.860 --> 15:21.890
See you later!

15:21.890 --> 15:23.320
Yeah. See you.

15:26.960 --> 15:30.050
So you finally found someone, Captain Rose.

15:30.050 --> 15:32.540
There you are, Brother!

15:32.540 --> 15:35.690
Seriously, going out on your own?
Do you <i>want</i> to die?!

15:35.690 --> 15:39.110
What? I'm not that weak.

15:39.370 --> 15:41.290
Why do you look so doubtful?

15:41.550 --> 15:44.740
More importantly, I met an interesting boy.

15:44.740 --> 15:46.950
Oh, yeah? How so?

15:46.950 --> 15:49.760
You'll see for yourself soon, Ururu.

15:50.140 --> 15:52.690
I'm sure you'll like him very much.

15:53.980 --> 15:56.990
Um, I'd like to enter...

15:56.990 --> 15:59.800
Can this little fellow come with me?

15:59.800 --> 16:02.480
You're Sir Usato from the 
Rescue Team, are you not?

16:02.480 --> 16:05.240
You may enter with the blue grizzly.

16:05.240 --> 16:09.230
Huh? Monsters are allowed
 into the castle? Really?

16:09.230 --> 16:14.140
Yes, Captain Rose has vouched 
for it. Please, go right in.

16:14.140 --> 16:16.020
Thank you very much.

16:16.970 --> 16:19.830
<i>A lot of people sure trust Rose...</i>

16:19.830 --> 16:21.380
Press farther forward!

16:21.380 --> 16:22.660
Yes, sir!

16:22.850 --> 16:25.130
You there! You're completely open below!

16:35.550 --> 16:39.250
It's Usato-kun! Hey!

16:40.970 --> 16:44.380
Hm? What is that fluffy blue creature?

16:44.950 --> 16:46.850
Oh, this little guy?

16:47.110 --> 16:49.570
It's a blue grizzly cub.

16:49.570 --> 16:55.680
Actually, I did some survival training in 
a forest infested with monsters, and...

16:55.680 --> 16:58.840
Are you listening, Inukami-senpai?

16:59.170 --> 17:01.550
U-Usato-kun...

17:03.090 --> 17:06.550
Is it all right if I touch it?!

17:06.550 --> 17:10.330
Yeah, go ahead. He's super tame.

17:10.330 --> 17:12.950
I'll heal you if you get bitten.

17:12.950 --> 17:15.450
You say some scary things.

17:15.450 --> 17:19.590
Well, I'm supposed to be the heroine, 
so animals should love m—

17:23.480 --> 17:26.630
H-He's just a little shy!

17:26.630 --> 17:27.970
Don't let it get you down!

17:28.360 --> 17:29.830
I'm not!

17:29.830 --> 17:32.830
I'm just savoring the feel of its toe beans!

17:32.830 --> 17:34.710
R-Really?

17:34.710 --> 17:37.310
Hey, why don't you try calling his name?

17:37.310 --> 17:40.570
I'm sure that'd do the trick!
His name is Blurin.

17:40.570 --> 17:44.340
Wow, what an excellent-sounding name!

17:44.340 --> 17:46.730
Let's be friends, Blurin—

17:48.930 --> 17:53.730
Maybe you just have a tainted soul, Senpai.

17:53.730 --> 17:57.300
Hey, Blurin. That's enough.

17:59.410 --> 18:03.160
Does this mean your soul is tainted, too?

18:03.160 --> 18:04.810
Seems that way.

18:05.680 --> 18:10.320
It feels like I haven't seen 
you in ages, Usato-kun.

18:10.320 --> 18:11.800
Right?

18:13.230 --> 18:14.400
Senpai, your hand...

18:14.850 --> 18:17.440
Oh, it isn't too bad.

18:17.440 --> 18:20.310
I just got overzealous 
with the sword training.

18:20.310 --> 18:22.940
You have to treat wounds properly.

18:26.760 --> 18:29.590
There. All healed.

18:30.710 --> 18:31.930
That's amazing.

18:32.160 --> 18:34.360
This much is nothing.

18:34.360 --> 18:35.410
Usato-kun...

18:35.880 --> 18:39.560
Did you come to see me today?

18:39.560 --> 18:42.190
Yeah. I came to visit you and Kazuki.

18:42.700 --> 18:46.240
Your overt honesty is your only flaw.

18:46.240 --> 18:47.110
Huh?

18:47.110 --> 18:50.950
Never mind. Kazuki-kun isn't here today.

18:50.950 --> 18:53.730
I'm sure he's outside the kingdom by now.

18:54.020 --> 18:54.710
Huh?

18:54.710 --> 18:59.950
He went to gain experience fighting 
monsters with Siglis and the others.

19:00.230 --> 19:05.630
Commander Siglis, is it true that the 
Demon Lord's army will attack soon?

19:05.630 --> 19:06.420
Yes.

19:06.870 --> 19:11.750
I'm sure they'll bring more 
powerful forces with them this time.

19:13.790 --> 19:17.710
However, we have you and Dame Suzune.

19:17.710 --> 19:21.390
The troops' morale is soaring now that 
we have two heroes on our side.

19:21.390 --> 19:23.150
Victory will be ours.

19:25.910 --> 19:29.950
You're right. I'll do my best.

19:29.950 --> 19:31.220
Hang wolves!

19:35.860 --> 19:37.130
Sir Kazuki!

19:37.530 --> 19:38.390
Yes!

19:40.930 --> 19:42.990
I hope Kazuki is all right.

19:43.280 --> 19:45.500
Well, it's only for a few days.

19:45.500 --> 19:50.070
Once Kazuki-kun returns, it'll be 
my turn to gain some experience.

19:50.070 --> 19:51.240
I can't wait.

19:51.580 --> 19:56.920
Yeah, I'm sure you'll have the time 
of your life. I can see it now.

19:56.920 --> 20:00.070
I wish you'd worry about me, too!

20:00.070 --> 20:02.270
Of course I'm worried about you.

20:02.270 --> 20:04.100
That was too half-hearted!

20:09.920 --> 20:11.230
Well, Senpai...

20:11.230 --> 20:12.630
I should get going.

20:12.630 --> 20:14.900
Yeah. Good luck on your training.

20:14.900 --> 20:16.560
Same to you. Later.

20:19.330 --> 20:24.240
<i>Usato-kun, have you noticed how 
frank you've grown with me?</i>

20:25.910 --> 20:29.080
<i>But that's fine. It's not such a bad feeling.</i>

20:29.660 --> 20:31.810
<i>Kazuki went out to train...</i>

20:31.810 --> 20:34.320
<i>Senpai is working her hardest, too.</i>

20:34.800 --> 20:37.760
<i>All because the day they go 
off to battle is drawing near.</i>

20:38.470 --> 20:41.910
<i>Since they're going to war, 
I want to help them.</i>

20:42.430 --> 20:45.480
<i>I don't want to hide in safety 
while they're in danger.</i>

20:46.360 --> 20:50.600
<i>Back home, all I could do was admire
people who could do things that I couldn't.</i>

20:51.500 --> 20:54.410
<i>But I'm not that person anymore.</i>

21:04.270 --> 21:06.030
Goodnight, Blurin.

21:17.370 --> 21:18.670
Usato.

21:19.240 --> 21:22.560
How was the training? 
Did you get used to it?

21:22.560 --> 21:24.180
Well...

21:24.180 --> 21:25.360
A bit, I guess.

21:25.360 --> 21:27.360
But I want to train a little longer.

21:27.360 --> 21:30.020
I see. Then keep going.

21:30.020 --> 21:30.940
Okay.

21:33.660 --> 21:35.180
Um, Captain Rose.

21:36.600 --> 21:38.800
About what you said yesterday...

21:39.270 --> 21:41.200
You told me to steel myself.

21:43.960 --> 21:49.410
I just barely survived 
against that snake monster,

21:49.410 --> 21:54.640
so I was honestly terrified when you
 mentioned the Demon Lord's army.

21:55.260 --> 22:00.160
If I didn't have to, I didn't want 
to set foot on the battlefield.

22:00.770 --> 22:04.580
But today, I found a feeling 
even stronger than that fear.

22:06.500 --> 22:08.350
I can't fight.

22:08.790 --> 22:09.560
I know.

22:10.190 --> 22:11.850
I can't kill anyone, either.

22:12.110 --> 22:13.000
I know.

22:13.520 --> 22:19.920
But I'll save Kazuki and Inukami-senpai,
and anyone else that only I can help.

22:21.650 --> 22:24.780
Because I'm part of the Rescue Team.

22:31.200 --> 22:32.540
That's perfect.

22:34.620 --> 22:37.160
We're going out there to save people.

22:37.620 --> 22:41.550
Knock out the would-be martyrs
 and bring them back.

22:41.550 --> 22:45.000
Snatch up the wounded that
the enemy is about to finish off.

22:45.470 --> 22:47.630
Keep those at death's door alive, 
even if it kills you.

22:47.920 --> 22:50.300
That's our job.

22:50.300 --> 22:52.220
Keep spouting those ideals.

22:52.450 --> 22:55.550
That's how the Rescue Team must be.

23:00.540 --> 23:02.020
Yes, Captain!

23:02.630 --> 23:08.550
<i>That moment was the first time I truly felt 
like I was a member of the Rescue Team.</i>

23:28.340 --> 23:29.440
Wake up.

23:29.440 --> 23:32.170
His Majesty sent a message over yesterday.

23:32.170 --> 23:34.050
He wants you to head out.

23:34.050 --> 23:37.690
What? Why didn't you tell me yesterday?

23:37.690 --> 23:42.040
He wants you to join Hero Suzune's 
training outside the castle.

23:42.040 --> 23:43.660
Inukami-senpai?

23:44.920 --> 23:45.970
Okay.
